    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASAN report confirms exactly the bug:\n\n- **Heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 2047** at `memchr` in `fgets_from_mem` (`tools.c:6684`)\n- The 50-byte input buffer (no newlines) causes `memchr` to scan 2047 bytes past the 50-byte allocation\n\nThe root cause: `fgets_from_mem` passes the output buffer capacity (`size`) to `memchr` as the scan length, instead of `MIN(size, end - *position)`. When the input data is shorter than the line buffer, `memchr` reads past the heap-allocated input.",
